    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Log wallet transfers to Google Sheets\n\n### How it works\nThe Qersh app on the merchant's phone posts every incoming wallet transfer (Vodafone Cash, Orange Cash, e& money, InstaPay) to the Qersh Trigger as a signed JSON delivery; the trigger verifies the signature and refuses anything else with 401. The connection test is answered without touching the sheet. Each transfer becomes one row: time, amount, payer, transaction id, wallet, risk. A later \"suspected forgery\" verdict marks the row. Repeated deliveries (the phone retries until it gets a 2xx) are found by delivery_id and not logged twice; the reply {\"status\":\"ok\"} tells the phone the delivery arrived.\n\n### Setup\n1. Add your **Qersh Webhook API** credential (install the Qersh community node first; on n8n Cloud open the nodes panel, \"More from the community\").\n2. Create a Google Sheet with a header row: received_at, amount, currency, payer_number, payer_name, provider_txn_id, wallet, risk, auto_confirm_ok, transfer_id, delivery_id, status. Select it and your Google credential in the three Google Sheets nodes.\n3. Activate the workflow, copy the trigger's **Production URL** into the Qersh app (More, Wallets, Add wallet, \"your store URL\"), then paste the key the phone shows into the credential. \"Test connection\" on the phone must say the signature was verified.\n\n### Customization tips\nAdd columns to the append node as you like (balance_after, payer handle). Keep \"Send sender details\" on \"full name and number\" in the wallet, or the payer number arrives masked. The phone retries a failed delivery for days, so a Sheets outage loses nothing.\n\nQersh (Qersh Pay) is a wallet notification relay, not a payment service provider. Docs: https://qersh.cfd/en/integrations/n8n",
        "height": 700,
        "width": 480,
        "color": 1
      },
